<title>GERMANY: West German Feb adjusted jobless falls 4,000.</title>
<headline>West German Feb adjusted jobless falls 4,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 Feb 97	  Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    3.257 million     3.266 million	2.961 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.018 million     3.022 million	2,749 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)		-4,000	  +67,000	  n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		10.6 pct	10.6 pct	 9.6 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	251,182	 224,457	  286,000</p>
<p> Vacancies		   290,025	 252,181	  277,340</p>
<p>Change in number in work Dec  96	Nov 96</p>
<p>				 -23,000	 -41,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
